<!--
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) Rikarin
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

    Doc 36 § F7 wave 6. The diagnostics row nine panels in this assembly build by hand — a stage, a
    message, and three lines of element building each. `AudioMixerView.cs` nominated it: "hoisting
    it into a part is a job for whoever ports the second of them, because doing it here would move
    pixels in a panel this change has not measured". `QueryView` and `GoapDomainView` are the second
    and the third, so this is that part, and the mixer moves onto it in the same commit with its
    dump re-checked.

    ⚠ **`@inherits Vixen.Ui.UiElement` and not `Control`**, for `FactRow`'s reason: a `Control` gives
    itself `variant-default` and `size-md` in `OnCreated`, and `analysis-list > analysis-row` is a
    plain element with neither. Two classes nothing styles would be two lines of difference in every
    dump for ever.

    ⚠ **The host tag *is* the `analysis-row`**, so `<AnalysisRow />` in a caller's `@for` stands
    exactly where `list.Add("analysis-row")` stood, as the same direct child of `analysis-list`. That
    is what makes the swap byte-neutral rather than merely equivalent — `analysis-list
    { flex-direction: column; gap: 2px }` reaches it and `analysis-row.error` still colours it.

    ⚠ **`ref` on both cells and a field behind each property, which is `FactRow`'s pattern and is
    needed for the same two reasons.** `<analysis-stage>@Stage</analysis-stage>` appends a `text`
    *child* rather than writing the cell's own `Text` — the ledger's shape 5 — and a C# caller may
    assign either property before the row is in a document, which `new AnalysisRow()` allows even
    though `Add<AnalysisRow>()` does not.

    ⚠ **`class` is the caller's and is not a parameter here.** `analysis-row.error` and
    `analysis-row.warning` are the two severity colours, `AddressableGroupsView` passes them
    positionally today, and `class` is one of markup's three universal attributes — so a caller
    writes `class="@note.Class"` on the tag and this file has no opinion about severity at all.
-->
@component AnalysisRow
@namespace Vixen.Editor.AssetEditors
@inherits Vixen.Ui.UiElement
@tag analysis-row
@using Vixen.Ui

<AnalysisStage ref="@StageCell" />
<AnalysisMessage ref="@MessageCell" />

@code {
    string stage = string.Empty;
    string detail = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The cell naming which part of the pipeline spoke.</summary>
    public UiElement StageCell { get; private set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>The cell holding what it said.</summary>
    public UiElement MessageCell { get; private set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>Which stage the complaint came from.</summary>
    public string Stage {
        get => stage;
        set {
            stage = value;

            if (StageCell is not null) {
                StageCell.Text = value;
            }
        }
    }

    /// <summary>And what it said.</summary>
    public string Message {
        get => detail;
        set {
            detail = value;

            if (MessageCell is not null) {
                MessageCell.Text = value;
            }
        }
    }

    partial void OnComposed() {
        StageCell.Text = stage;
        MessageCell.Text = detail;
    }
}
